# Party banter while exploring Death House (and the road into it). Each node is one short exchange; its opening
# `if` is the gate. The game plays an eligible node (gate true) at a quiet moment, once each.
# Pregen voices: docs/voice/{godrick_pendlebrook, liriel_dawnsong, thistle, ratatoille, wren_featherfoot,
# kip_smudgewick}.md. Class, species and background lines are written so any such character could say them.

~ bt_too_clean
if name:ratatoille and name:wren_featherfoot and visited:dh_main_hall and not flag.death_house_completed
  interject name:ratatoille: Not a speck of dust. Not one. I have never been so frightened by good housekeeping.
  interject name:wren_featherfoot: Bet you checked the corners anyway.
  interject name:ratatoille: I have checked the corners. The corners are immaculate.
endif
-> END

~ bt_wolves_on_the_road
if flag.mists_wolves_cowed and visited:death_house_ground and class:fighter and class:cleric
  interject class:fighter: Those wolves gave way like a picket line. Someone's expecting us.
  interject class:cleric: Then let's be late. Rudely, unforgivably late.
endif
-> END

~ bt_wolf_blood
if flag.mists_wolves_fought and visited:dh_den and name:thistle and name:ratatoille
  interject name:thistle: Eleven wolf heads on that wall. Wolves on the road, waiting for us. Wolves remember.
  interject name:ratatoille: A feud, then. The house hunted someone's wolves, and now someone's wolves hunt the house's guests.
endif
-> END

~ bt_locked_from_outside
if visited:dh_childrens_room and name:thistle and name:godrick_pendlebrook
  interject name:thistle: Lock's on the outside. Of a little one's room. I hate that. I hate that.
  interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Then I'll take the door off its hinges. No hinges, no lock. Just a plank.
  interject name:thistle: ...Good. Do it.
endif
-> END

~ bt_nursery_locks
if visited:dh_childrens_room and class:rogue
  interject class:rogue: Locks on the outside of a children's door. Whoever fitted those knew exactly what they were for.
endif
-> END

~ bt_theology_of_debt
if flag.death_house_read_strahd_letter and name:kip_smudgewick and name:liriel_dawnsong
  interject name:kip_smudgewick: His letter treats worship like a debt. I know that kind of letter. I've had that kind of letter.
  interject name:liriel_dawnsong: The Morninglord has never once sent me a bill, Kip. He sends the morning. Every morning. Free.
  interject name:kip_smudgewick: No obligation?
  interject name:liriel_dawnsong: None at all.
endif
-> END

~ bt_the_signature
if flag.death_house_read_strahd_letter and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:wren_featherfoot
  interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: What's it say at the bottom? My eyes are tired.
  interject name:wren_featherfoot: Just an S. Signed like he's sure we'll know him.
  interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Do we?
  interject name:wren_featherfoot: We will.
endif
-> END

~ bt_windmill
if flag.death_house_found_deeds and name:ratatoille and name:kip_smudgewick
  interject name:ratatoille: A deed to a windmill. A windmill means flour. Flour means pastry. Kip, we could have a shop.
  interject name:kip_smudgewick: Apricot tarts. You bake, I sell. After. If there's an after.
  interject name:ratatoille: There will be an after. I have foreseen it. Roughly.
endif
-> END

~ bt_dwarf_stonework
if visited:dh_family_crypts and species:dwarf
  interject species:dwarf: Good stonework, all of it. Somebody with a real chisel cut these crypts. Pity about the tenants.
endif
-> END

~ bt_elf_portraits
if visited:dh_upper_hall and species:elf
  interject species:elf: My grandmother wore a collar like that in her portrait. She said it was embarrassing then, too.
endif
-> END

~ bt_halfling_dumbwaiter
if visited:dh_kitchen and species:halfling and class:fighter
  interject species:halfling: I'd fit in that dumbwaiter, you know.
  interject class:fighter: You are not getting in the dumbwaiter.
  interject species:halfling: I said I'd fit. I didn't say I'd go. ...I might go.
endif
-> END

~ bt_soldier_barracks
if visited:dh_cult_dormitory and background:soldier
  interject background:soldier: Bunks in rows, kit on pegs, a roster on the wall. They ran it like a barracks. That's how you get ordinary people to do this.
endif
-> END

~ bt_criminal_keepsakes
if visited:dh_lower_landing and background:criminal
  interject background:criminal: Alcoves full of other people's keepsakes. The cult robbed its dead and kept the pieces like relics. I'm not taking any of those. Not those.
endif
-> END

~ bt_children_truth
if flag.death_house_children_truth and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:liriel_dawnsong
  interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: They were waiting for somebody to come. Somebody came. It's us. We're late, but we came.
  interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Then let's not keep them waiting any longer.
endif
-> END

~ bt_humming
if flag.death_house_children_riding and not flag.death_house_children_at_rest
  Narrator: One of you is humming a nursery tune that none of you know.
  Player: Who's humming?
  Narrator: Nobody answers, and the humming stops. Then, very quietly, someone giggles.
endif
-> END

~ bt_lure
if flag.death_house_saw_through_lure and class:cleric and class:wizard
  interject class:cleric: The children in the road were bait. The house dangles them and waits.
  interject class:wizard: An old trick. Effective, apparently. We're inside.
endif
-> END

~ bt_escape_chair
if flag.death_house_refused and not flag.death_house_completed and name:kip_smudgewick and name:thistle
  interject name:kip_smudgewick: Keep moving. Don't touch anything. Please.
  interject name:thistle: Not touching anything.
  interject name:kip_smudgewick: You're carrying a chair.
  interject name:thistle: Good chair. Mine.
endif
-> END

~ bt_lorghoth_slain
if flag.death_house_lorghoth_slain and class:fighter and class:wizard
  interject class:fighter: We killed the thing in the basement.
  interject class:wizard: We killed a thing in the basement. I'd hesitate to call it the thing.
endif
-> END

~ bt_after_the_altar
if flag.death_house_sacrificed
  Narrator: Nobody says the number aloud anymore. Nobody needs to.
endif
-> END
